    "The contract reservations table gives a demand per product per quarter — should I treat these as minimum deliveries that must be met each quarter (with any extra production allowed to be carried as inventory), or as exact quantities that must be delivered in that quarter (so producing more than the reservation in a quarter is not allowed)?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single policy choice regarding how to interpret the contract reservations (minimum vs. exact), which constitutes one semantically independent question."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
