    "When a delivery is delayed, how should I model the delay cost — specifically, if a unit of product I that was due in quarter 1 is finally delivered in quarter 3, is the delay cost 20 yuan × 2 quarters (i.e., 20 yuan for each quarter it was late), or is it a flat 20 yuan per unit regardless of how many quarters late it is?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single policy choice regarding the calculation method for delay costs (per-quarter vs. flat), which constitutes one semantically independent question."
}

